  ===========================================================================

  This report's value is out of all proportion to its size, and the reason is
  worth stating precisely so it is never dropped for being small.

  The class covered here exercises the transformer that projects lock state into
  the external search platform, whose wire behaviour, meaning the same
  endpoints, the same formats and the same authentication, must be preserved. It
  uses NEITHER mocking framework, because it constructs the transformer
  directly. It imports no name from the javax namespace. It was untouched by the
  change set's test rewrites. And the search client it ultimately serves is held
  at its existing version under the contrapositive recorded in section 5.

  Every variable except the runtime is therefore held still, so any difference
  between this report and its baseline twin points at the RUNTIME ALONE. That is
  what makes it a control, and that is what makes the tie-breaker rule
  meaningful for this module rather than merely invoked. The sibling report
  cannot play that role: its class was rewritten onto a different mocking
  mechanism, so a difference there has two candidate causes rather than one.

  It also supports the search round trip smoke flow, whose criterion is an
  identical result set and identical ranking, and it stands alongside the
  sibling report as the module level evidence that object lock semantics, which
  underpin concurrent edit behaviour, are preserved unchanged.

